## Summary
A judge ruled that Florida International University (FIU) violated the free speech rights of its students. The decision was reported by Inside Higher Ed on August 25, 2026, authored by Kathryn Palmer. This highlights legal challenges to student expression in academic institutions.

## Key Points
- Judge ruled FIU violated student free speech rights.
- The case involves legal issues regarding student expression at a major university in South Florida.
- Reported by Inside Higher Ed, with author Kathryn Palmer.
- The ruling occurred in August 2026, indicating recent legal developments.


